= Displaying Profile Details =

To display a profile:
<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-show userKey
-----------------
Profile "userKey"
-----------------
  Profile ID: userKey
  Status: Enabled
  Properties:
    op.enroll.userKey.auth.enable: true
    op.enroll.userKey.auth.id: ldap1
    ...
</pre>

To save a profile into a file:

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-show userKey --output userKey.xml
-----------------------------------------
Stored profile "userKey" into userKey.xml
-----------------------------------------
</pre>

The profile will be stored in XML format:

<pre>
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<Profile id="userKey" xmlns:ns2="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
    <Link href="https://server.example.com:8443/tps/rest/profiles/userKey" rel="self"/>
    <Properties>
        <Property name="op.enroll.userKey.auth.enable">true</Property>
        <Property name="op.enroll.userKey.auth.id">ldap1</Property>
        ...
    </Properties>
    <Status>Enabled</Status>
</Profile>
</pre>

= Adding a Profile =

Prepare a profile in a file (or copy from an existing profile):

<pre>
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<Profile id="test" xmlns:ns2="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
    <Link href="https://server.example.com:8443/tps/rest/profiles/test" rel="self"/>
    <Properties>
        <Property name="op.enroll.test.auth.enable">true</Property>
        <Property name="op.enroll.test.auth.id">ldap1</Property>
        ...
    </Properties>
    <Status>Enabled</Status>
</Profile>
</pre>

Add the profile with the following command.

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-add --input test.xml
</pre>

= Modify a Profile =

To disable a profile:

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-mod test --action disable
</pre>

To enable a profile:

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-mod test --action enable
</pre>

To update a profile, download the existing profile into a file using the tps-profile-show command, make the modifications in the file, then reupload the file with the following command:

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-mod test --input test.xml
</pre>

= Deleting a Profile =

To delete a profile, make sure it is disabled, then execute the following command:

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias/ -c Secret.123 -n caadmin tps-profile-del test
----------------------
Deleted profile "test"
----------------------
</pre>

